<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Haji Ebrahim Khan Kalantar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1745">1745</a>–<a href="/years/1801">1801</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Ebrahim Khan Etemad od-Dowleh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Haji Ebrahim Khan Kalantar was the kalantar (mayor) of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiraz">Shiraz</a> who in 1791 betrayed the last Zand ruler, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lotf-ali-khan">Lotf Ali Khan</a>, and handed the city to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agha-mohammad-khan-qajar">Agha Mohammad Khan Qajar</a>. He became the first grand <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajar dynasty</a> and kept the post under Fath-Ali Shah, until the shah, fearing his power, had him and his family seized and executed in 1801.</p></div>
